<article class="env-remark" id="03FF">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03FF">Remark <span data-tag="03FF">34.11.1</span>.</a> Take any category $\mathit{Sch}_\alpha $ constructed as in Sets, Lemma <a href="/tag/000J" data-tag="000J">3.9.2</a> starting with the set of schemes $\{ X, Y, S\} $. Choose any set of coverings $\text{Cov}_{fppf}$ on $\mathit{Sch}_\alpha $ as in Sets, Lemma <a href="/tag/000X" data-tag="000X">3.11.1</a> starting with the category $\mathit{Sch}_\alpha $ and the class of fppf coverings. Let $\mathit{Sch}_{fppf}$ denote the big fppf site so obtained. Next, for $\tau \in \{ Zariski, {\acute{e}tale}, smooth, syntomic\} $ let $\mathit{Sch}_\tau $ have the same underlying category as $\mathit{Sch}_{fppf}$ with coverings $\text{Cov}_\tau \subset \text{Cov}_{fppf}$ simply the subset of $\tau $-coverings. It is straightforward to check that this gives rise to a big site $\mathit{Sch}_\tau $. </p>
